  - "Pisano period"
  - "Lucas sequences"
abstract: >
  This preprint evaluates the quadratic character sum
  S(p)=sum_{n=1}^{p-1} chi_p(F_n) under the full-rank hypothesis
  alpha(p)=p-1, where alpha(p) is the rank of apparition of p in the
  Fibonacci sequence. It proves that p is congruent to 11 or 19 modulo 20
  and that the sum is respectively +1 or -1. The proof derives a
  primitive-root parametrization from the full-rank condition, reduces the
  sum to a quadratic character of a difference of roots of x^2-x-1, and
  determines the remaining sign by a cyclotomic discriminant argument.
